WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.039 --> 00:00:07.704
Kopp and Humm weren't the only ones looking for a cure.

2
00:00:07.705 --> 00:00:11.367
The palace servants loved the lighthearted princess.

3
00:00:11.368 --> 00:00:19.261
She made them laugh and feel happy.

4
00:00:19.262 --> 00:00:23.307
"I know what will help her," a servant told Nanny.

5
00:00:23.308 --> 00:00:27.242
"Falling in love with a handsome prince."

6
00:00:27.243 --> 00:00:29.454
Nanny shook her head.

7
00:00:29.455 --> 00:00:34.384
"Don't you remember? The princess has no gravity.

8
00:00:34.385 --> 00:00:39.675
She can't fall into anything!"

9
00:00:39.676 --> 00:00:44.611
Actually, reader, the princess was already in love.

10
00:00:44.612 --> 00:00:47.034
But it wasn't with a prince.

11
00:00:47.035 --> 00:00:51.800
It was with the palace's lake.

12
00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:56.733
It started when Ellen accidentally fell in the water.

13
00:00:56.734 --> 00:00:59.939
The family was boating on the lake.

14
00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:06.980
Ellen suddenly spotted a friend's boat across the lake.

15
00:01:06.981 --> 00:01:13.365
"Papa, I want to go on Mary's boat. Can you help me?"

16
00:01:13.366 --> 00:01:16.691
"Of course." The king picked her up.

17
00:01:16.692 --> 00:01:20.475
He carried her to the side of the boat when—

18
00:01:20.476 --> 00:01:24.549
boompf! He tripped, and Ellen splashed into the

19
00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:27.431
water. "She'll drown!" the king

20
00:01:27.432 --> 00:01:29.428
cried. "She can't

21
00:01:29.429 --> 00:01:36.268
swim!" "I'll save her, Your Majesty!" A servant dived into the

22
00:01:36.269 --> 00:01:42.349
water. But when the servant came back up, his arms were

23
00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:47.536
empty. A second later the princess popped up—on the other side of the lake.

24
00:01:47.537 --> 00:01:55.598
"Here I am!" she yelled, laughing.

25
00:01:55.599 --> 00:01:59.904
The servant tried to get her, but she swam away.

26
00:01:59.905 --> 00:02:12.951
For hours, she swam around the lake like a swan.

27
00:02:12.952 --> 00:02:17.789
In the water gravity didn't matter.

28
00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:23.487
For the first time, Ellen felt truly free to move on her own.

29
00:02:23.488 --> 00:02:29.186
After this event all Ellen wanted to do was swim.

30
00:02:29.187 --> 00:02:35.216
In the summer she swam all day long.

31
00:02:35.217 --> 00:02:42.889
In the winter servants broke the ice for her.

32
00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:52.878
At night she stared out her bedroom window, missing the lake.

33
00:02:52.879 --> 00:03:01.594
The philosophers watched Ellen closely.

34
00:03:01.595 --> 00:03:04.928
Soon they both had the same thought.

35
00:03:04.929 --> 00:03:07.462
"That's it!" Kopp shouted.

36
00:03:07.463 --> 00:03:10.430
"Yes!" Humm cried.

37
00:03:10.431 --> 00:03:13.873
They rushed to tell the king and queen.

38
00:03:13.874 --> 00:03:20.510
"Your Majesties! We have found a cure for the princess!" Kopp said.

39
00:03:20.511 --> 00:03:23.977
"A wonderful cure! It's water!"

40
00:03:23.978 --> 00:03:26.799
"Water?" The king frowned.

41
00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:30.718
"She swims all the time. Water hasn't cured her yet."

42
00:03:30.719 --> 00:03:33.466
"No," Kopp said impatiently.

43
00:03:33.467 --> 00:03:38.556
"She needs water from inside herself. The water must come from—"

44
00:03:38.557 --> 00:03:45.928
"Tears!" Humm said. "We must make Ellen cry!"

